; REQUIRES: minisat
; RUN: %solver -d --simplifying-minisat --lazy-write-reads-depth=0 %s | %OutputCheck %s
; CHECK: ^sat
;
; A chain row refined over more than one round, on a SAT backend that
; eliminates variables. Sixteen reads share a three-store may-alias chain,
; so the later ones are abstracted to rows (depth 0 abstracts every
; may-alias level; the first few reads stay eager). Each read may hit any
; of the three stores but must not return the value of the top two, and
; the top index is pinned to zero so the first candidate resolves every
; row at level 0, which the lemma for that level then rules out. The next
; candidate resolves deeper, and its path lemma names the level-0 guard
; again.
;
; emitChainReadLemmas() caches a row's guard equality variables across
; rounds so a deep row does not rebuild its comparison circuits, but until
; the guards were frozen the simplifying MiniSat was free to eliminate a
; guard during the solve between two rounds. The next round's lemma then
; aborted in SimpSolver::addClause_ on `!isEliminated(var(ps[i]))'; the
; release build instead accepted a clause over a variable it had already
; resolved away, which left the lemma vacuous and the search churning.
(set-logic QF_ABV)
(declare-fun a () (Array (_ BitVec 8) (_ BitVec 8)))
(declare-fun i0 () (_ BitVec 8))
(declare-fun v0 () (_ BitVec 8))
(declare-fun i1 () (_ BitVec 8))
(declare-fun v1 () (_ BitVec 8))
(declare-fun i2 () (_ BitVec 8))
(declare-fun v2 () (_ BitVec 8))
(declare-fun j0 () (_ BitVec 8))
(declare-fun r0 () (_ BitVec 8))
(assert (= r0 (select (store (store (store a i2 v2) i1 v1) i0 v0) j0)))
(assert (or (= j0 i0) (= j0 i1) (= j0 i2)))
(assert (distinct r0 v0))
(assert (distinct r0 v1))
(declare-fun j1 () (_ BitVec 8))
(declare-fun r1 () (_ BitVec 8))
(assert (= r1 (select (store (store (store a i2 v2) i1 v1) i0 v0) j1)))
